# Normalize line endings on checkout, independent of any runner's core.autocrlf default.
#
# Root cause this file fixes: actions/checkout on a Windows runner (windows-2025) inherits the
# runner image's core.autocrlf=true, and this repo carried no .gitattributes, so every text
# file -- including flake.nix -- was checked out with CRLF line endings. A `pkgs.runCommand`
# derivation embeds its Nix builder shell script literally inside the .nix file, so a
# CRLF-corrupted flake.nix corrupts that embedded script too, and the derivation's
# builder failed with exit code 127: "/build/.attr-...: line 1: $'\r': command not found". The
# same corruption blocks every `nix develop` invocation on `.github/workflows/ci-windows.yml`'s
# runs (its wsl2-probe job's Probe C and Probe D, and its `build` job's `lake build` step --
# `lake build` depends on `nix develop .#build`), independent of WSL2 itself: this is a
# checkout-normalization bug, not a WSL2/Nix capability limit. See `docs/ci.md`'s Windows
# coverage notes and `docs/setup-without-nix.md`'s Windows section for the evidence trail.
#
# `eol=lf` forces LF in the working directory regardless of core.autocrlf/core.eol (see
# `git help gitattributes`, "eol" attribute) -- it is the fix, not merely a mitigation, and it
# protects every checkout of this repo, not only ci-windows.yml's: a Windows contributor
# cloning locally with Git's default autocrlf=true would hit the identical builder failure
# without this file. A per-workflow `git config --global core.autocrlf false` step before
# actions/checkout was considered and deliberately not added in addition to this file: it would
# protect only ci-windows.yml's own checkout, leaving every other entry point (a local Windows
# clone, a future Windows-runner workflow) exposed to the same bug this file already closes
# repo-wide.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit binary declarations for the repository's known non-text assets, so `text=auto`'s
# content sniffing is never the only thing preventing a corrupting normalization attempt.
*.pdf -text
*.png -text
*.jpg -text
*.jpeg -text
*.gif -text
*.ico -text
*.woff -text
*.woff2 -text
*.ttf -text
*.otf -text
*.eot -text
